@ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5291

GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### All batches (closest expiry first)
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches

### Only Active batches
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches?status=Active

### Batches behind a dashboard card (Expired, Within3Days, Within4To7Days)
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches?bucket=Within3Days

### Invalid status: should return 400
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches?status=Expired

###

### Add a batch (valid)
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Juhayna Milk 1L",
  "category": "Dairy",
  "quantity": 24,
  "costPricePiasters": 3000,
  "unitPricePiasters": 3500,
  "expiryDate": "2026-11-15"
}

### Add a batch (invalid: should return 400 with errors)
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "",
  "category": "Dairy",
  "quantity": 0,
  "costPricePiasters": 3000,
  "unitPricePiasters": -5,
  "expiryDate": "2026-11-15"
}

### Discount batch 1 (milk) to 28 EGP
PATCH {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches/1/action
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "Discount",
  "discountPricePiasters": 2800
}

### Sell batch 1
PATCH {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches/1/action
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "Sell"
}

### Waste batch 2 (bread) because it expired
PATCH {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/batches/2/action
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "Waste",
  "wasteReason": "Expired"
}

### Dashboard: expired / within 3 days / within 4 to 7 days
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/dashboard

### Losses report for a month (waste by category, biggest loss first)
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/reports/losses?month=2026-11

### Losses report for the current month
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/reports/losses

### Demo seed: DELETES all batches, then adds realistic demo data (Development only)
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/demo/seed

###

# ---------- Cartons (new QR flow) ----------
# qrText is the raw text inside the QR, so its quotes are escaped (\") inside this JSON body.

### 1) New product, no selling price: 400 "New product: enter the selling price of one piece."
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-001\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":12,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-A\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-01\",\"exp\":\"2027-05-01\",\"cost\":40000}"
}

### 2) Same carton WITH a selling price (5.50 EGP per piece): 201, product + carton created, 120 pieces
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-001\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":12,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-A\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-01\",\"exp\":\"2027-05-01\",\"cost\":40000}",
  "sellingPricePiasters": 550
}

### 3) Scan the same carton again: 409 with receivedAt
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-001\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":12,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-A\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-01\",\"exp\":\"2027-05-01\",\"cost\":40000}",
  "sellingPricePiasters": 550
}

### 4) Another carton of the SAME product, no price needed now: 201, reuses the product
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-002\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":12,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-B\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-05\",\"exp\":\"2027-05-05\",\"cost\":40000}"
}

### 5) Not our QR (a website link): 400 "This QR is not an Expiry Tracker carton label."
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "https://example.com"
}

### 6) Our format but wrong values (expiry before production, 0 boxes): 400 with field errors
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-003\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":0,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-C\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-01\",\"exp\":\"2026-10-01\",\"cost\":40000}"
}

###

# ---------- Carton preview (reads the label, saves NOTHING) ----------

### 7) Preview a carton we already received: 200, alreadyReceivedAt is set, needsSellingPrice = false
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-001\",\"barcode\":\"6221234567890\",\"name\":\"Chocolate biscuit\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":12,\"perBox\":10,\"lot\":\"L-2611-A\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-01\",\"exp\":\"2027-05-01\",\"cost\":40000}"
}

### 8) Preview a NEW product's carton: 200, needsSellingPrice = true, alreadyReceivedAt = null
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"test-carton-101\",\"barcode\":\"6229876543210\",\"name\":\"Vanilla wafer\",\"category\":\"Snacks\",\"boxes\":24,\"perBox\":6,\"lot\":\"W-2611-A\",\"mfg\":\"2026-11-03\",\"exp\":\"2026-11-20\",\"cost\":36000}"
}

### 9) Preview a bad QR: 400, same message as scan
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cartons/scan/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "qrText": "https://example.com"
}

###

# ---------- Factory labels (signed QRs) ----------
# Since labels are signed, the hand-written qrText samples above now return 400
# "not a carton label". Make real ones here, then copy a qrText into a scan request.

### Create 3 labels: 201 with labels[].qrText (each one signed, ids CT-ED261107-0001..0003)
POST {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/labels/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productName": "Edita Molto Croissant",
  "barcode": "6223001360210",
  "category": "Snacks",
  "boxesCount": 12,
  "piecesPerBox": 10,
  "lotNumber": "ED-2611-07",
  "productionDate": "2026-11-01",
  "expiryDate": "2026-11-14",
  "costPiasters": 84000,
  "cartonCount": 3
}

### Load a job again (the print preview page does this): 200, same ids and signatures
GET {{ExpiryTracker.Api_HostAddress}}/api/labels/jobs/1

###
